+# tark_xlit
+
+Tark's on-device transliteration for the address bar: type `namaste`, get
+`नमस्ते` offered next to the search row, in the Indian languages you have
+set in Tark's language settings.
+
+The component holds:
+
+- `languages.{h,cc}`: the 20 supported languages (accept-language code,
+  IndicXlit tag, script, name in its own script from CLDR), script detection,
+  the choice of which languages to offer rows for, the test for "could this be
+  an Indian-language word typed in Latin letters", and the choice of
+  Wikipedia language for `@wiki`.
+- `model.{h,cc}`: IndicXlit itself, a fairseq transformer read from the TXLM
+  blob into float32 and run with Accelerate's BLAS, and fairseq's beam search
+  (four candidates per word). `utils/xlit_reference.py` is its specification;
+  `test/data/golden.tsv` is that reference's output, and the tests check
+  every line of it.
+- `word_list.{h,cc}`: the per-language word-frequency lists and the
+  common-English list (TXLW blob), and IndicXlit's dictionary rescoring.
+- `transliterator.{h,cc}`: a typed phrase to the phrase in a script. Words on
+  the common-English list stay as typed, the others become the model's top
+  candidate after rescoring, with a per-instance cache of 5,000 words.
+  `LoadResourcesFromBundle()` loads the model and word lists from `indicxlit/`
+  in the app's assets into a `Resources` that any number of `Transliterator`s
+  share read-only, each with its own cache; `LoadFromBundle()` builds one
+  `Transliterator` over them. Both block on file IO, so call them off the UI
+  thread.
+- `xlit_bench.cc`: `tark_xlit_bench` prints p50/p95 of `Phrase` for uncached
+  words in three languages; the budget is 50 ms at p95.
+
+The model is AI4Bharat's IndicXlit (MIT licence, `third_party/indicxlit`),
+converted at setup into a flat weight file that ships inside the app and runs
+on the CPU. **This component never touches the network.** It has no
+dependency on any networking, URL-loading or profile code, and the model is
+read from the app bundle, never downloaded at run time.
+
+`tark_xlit_unittests` tests it without building the browser:
+
+```sh
+ninja -C out/Default tark_xlit_unittests && out/Default/tark_xlit_unittests
+```
+
+The latency check:
+
+```sh
+ninja -C out/Default tark_xlit_bench && out/Default/tark_xlit_bench
+```
